                description: r#"The first cut captured a full SceneRecord on every operation context: every call, every script run pass, and every frame while F3 search is open. The orchestrator rejected that. The registry needed a way to build a costly mirror only when the operation that reads it may run."#,
                decision: true,
                options: [
                    (
                        label: "Gated fillers in gradiance-op",
                        caption: r#"OpContextFillers::add_for(ops, filler) runs only for a context built by OpContext::build_for with a predicate naming one of ops. invoke and invoke_as pass their own id; a script pass passes the ids whose Lisp verb its sources name as a whole token (bridge::mentions); F3 search and the groups filter use OpContext::build, which runs no gated filler. A gated op lowered without its mirror fails with MissingMirror. General, small, unit-tested; scene.dump stays a synchronous query."#,
                    ),
                    (
                        label: "Dump as a request answered later",
                        caption: r#"scene.dump lowers to a request persist drains. Cost: the caller gets no value from the call, so a remote client would need a second read path."#,
                    ),
                    (
                        label: "A cheap flag the filler checks",
                        caption: r#"A resource flag set before lowering scene.dump. Cost: every doorway must remember to set it; nothing general."#,
                    ),
                ],
            ),
